# Ownership for the merge gate on main.
#
# THIS FILE IS HALF OF A GATE, AND THE OTHER HALF IS A REPOSITORY SETTING.
# main's ruleset requires a pull request whose review comes from a code owner;
# that requirement resolves to nobody on any path this file does not cover, so
# the `*` line below is what makes "reviewed by a code owner" mean "reviewed".
# Narrowing it to a path list would silently exempt every path not on the list.
#
# NAME A TEAM OR A USER, NEVER AN ORGANIZATION. `@buildfoundry-nz` is an
# organization, not a team, and GitHub resolves it to no owner at all — a
# CODEOWNERS file written that way is syntactically fine, renders in the UI as
# an error nobody reads, and requires the approval of an empty set. That is not
# hypothetical: it is the live state of the CODEOWNERS in this repository's
# validating target, where all 44 protected-surface lines name the organization
# and `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/codeowners/errors` answers with 38 "Unknown
# owner" errors. internal/repoproof/codeowners_test.go fails this file if an
# owner is spelled that way here.
#
# The API above is also how this file is checked against the real repository,
# and it is the only way: an owner that does not exist, or that exists without
# write access, is not visible in the file's text.
* @buildfoundry-nz/engineering
